## Project Overview
- App: SentryLinux — AI-augmented endpoint security hub, automated hardening console, and network sentry for Ubuntu 24.04 LTS.
- Platform: Native Ubuntu Desktop Application (Tauri v2 + React 19)
- Preferred Language: Rust + Tauri v2 (GTK4 / Libadwaita UI layout; Rust telemetry daemon (eBPF/auditd, tokio, aya-rs); Python 3.12 bindings; google-genai SDK for Gemini 3.8 Flash triage and Gemini 3.1 Pro forensic reasoning; D-Bus / polkit execution bridge.)
- Idea: SentryLinux unifies Ubuntu's fragmented CLI security ecosystem—auditd, AppArmor, Lynis, UFW, OpenSnitch, Fail2ban, Suricata, ClamAV, LMD, RKhunter, chkrootkit, AIDE, Debsums, USBGuard, and NextDNS—into a native desktop workstation. 

Instead of draining system resources training heavy ML models locally, SentryLinux employs an intelligent dual-model AI tier: Gemini 3.8 Flash delivers sub-second event triage, live outbound socket evaluation, and structured Pydantic alerts, while Gemini 3.1 Pro performs cross-tool attack correlation, rootkit false-positive verification against signed package manifests, and forensic post-mortems. 

The app resolves the chronic Linux networking friction between Proton VPN and NextDNS via dynamic resolvectl interface scoping and automated linked IP synchronization, and features a granular USG CIS benchmark checklist with interactive diff previews prior to privileged execution.

