8. Systemd Service Isolation & Exposure Auditing
Automated systemd-analyze security Pipeline:

Ingests and parses Ubuntu’s native service exposure ratings, scoring every running system and user daemon on an exposure scale from 0.0 (Hardened) to 10.0 (Exposed/Unsafe).

Evaluates critical sandbox primitives per service: ProtectSystem=strict, ProtectHome=yes, NoNewPrivileges=yes, PrivateTmp=yes, CapabilityBoundingSet=, and RestrictRealtime=yes.

AI-Guided Systemd Drop-In Generator:

Instead of manually crafting systemd overrides, Gemini analyzes the service’s runtime dependencies and drafts a safe drop-in unit file (/etc/systemd/system/<service>.d/99-hardening.conf).

Features a simulated run to ensure tightening socket or filesystem restrictions will not break system operations before writing to disk.

9. Boot Chain, Firmware & Hardware-Rooted Integrity
TPM 2.0 PCR Attestation Monitor:

Monitors Platform Configuration Registers (PCR 0, 2, 4, 7) via tpm2-tools to detect unauthorized modifications to the UEFI firmware, Option ROMs, bootloader (GRUB), or kernel command lines before the OS boots.

Alerts on unexpected PCR hash drift that could indicate evil maid attacks, firmware implants, or unauthorized boot tampering.

LUKS Keyslot & FDE Sentry:

Audits Full Disk Encryption key slots via cryptsetup luksDump, tracking active key slots, wipe commands, and passphrases.

Alerts immediately if an unrecognized encryption key, recovery pin, or Clevis/Tang binding is added to the partition header.

Secure Boot & Kernel Lockdown Enforcer:

Visual status monitor tracking mokutil and Machine Owner Keys (MOK).

Verifies kernel lockdown status (kernel.lockdown=integrity or confidentiality) to guarantee unsigned kernel modules or direct /dev/mem memory writes cannot bypass system security.

10. Desktop Isolation, Portals & Sandboxing
Native Flatpak Permission Manager (Flatseal Integration):

Built-in viewer and editor auditing sandbox overrides across installed Flatpak applications.

Toggles for filesystem escape hatches (filesystem=host, filesystem=home), X11 display socket access, device subsystem visibility, and background execution permissions.

Wayland & XDG Portal Snoop Guard:

Real-time watchdog over the XDG Desktop Portal D-Bus interface.

Triggers desktop warnings whenever an unprivileged application attempts screen casting, remote desktop control, global input sniffing, or clipboard polling under Wayland.

Unprivileged Landlock & Seccomp Launchpad:

"Run with Landlock" context menu option: launches untrusted scripts or ad-hoc binaries locked strictly to their immediate working directory without requiring root privileges.

